{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Moses." "<b>For a hand is on the throne of Yah.</b> The hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, was raised to swear by His throne that there be war and everlasting enmity against Amalek. And why is it written כֵּס and not כִּסֵּא? And the Name too is split in half? The Holy One, blessed be He, swore that His name is not whole and His throne is not whole until he utterly blots out the name of Amalek; and when his name is blotted out, the Name will be whole and the throne whole — as it says: ״הָאוֹיֵב תַּמּוּ חֳרָבוֹת לָנֶצַח״ (Psalms 9). This is Amalek, of whom it is written: ״וְעֶבְרָתוֹ שְׁמָרָה נֶצַח״ (Amos 1). ״וְעָרִים נָתַשְׁתָּ אָבַד זִכְרָם הֵמָּה״ (Psalms, same chapter) — what does it say after it? ״וַה' לְעוֹלָם יֵשֵׁב״ — behold, the Name is whole; ״כּוֹנֵן לַמִּשְׁפָּט כִּסְאוֹ״ — behold, His throne is whole."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:55.592174019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}